 "text": "Hi, how are you holding up? That's usually the pins on the chain rubbing against the cogs. You can stop at any shop and get a new one, or you can do it at home. It' hold for a few days, but it won't last and it reek. Better to buy a cheap new one, they' cheap and it' worth it not smell like food. Find which direction the sprockets on the wheel spin and which way the chain comes off. Then thread it through the big pin and push it back on. Get the ends parallel and tight. Clean it with mild soap, but don' use anything abrasive. A little goes a long way. Wring the water out and dry it with a clean cloth.",
